Tue Oct 27 12:00:00 UTC 2026 - Matthias Eckermann <mge@suse.com>

- gateway: ship an example systemd drop-in for cgroup controller
  delegation (/usr/share/openshell-gateway/80-openshell-delegate.conf,
  Delegate=pids memory cpu). SUSE delegates no controller to user
  sessions; without cpu, memory and pids the Podman driver's limits
  make "openshell sandbox create" fail ("memory.swap.max: no such
  file or directory"). The administrator activates the file; the
  package never writes to /etc.
- gateway: README.SUSE with the host prerequisites on SUSE

